From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: EDEN_NX2_NULL_SLOTS logs or rebuilds compute programs translated with null list pointers

Core patch, on the T45 series or mig020-core. Off unless the switch is set. Port of the runtime half of
Lichii PR 395 (atk3001, open), for our compute cache, which has no cache entry struct.

A native program's pointer slot that holds null at translation gets no binding, its accesses are lost,
and vulkan.bin keeps that answer for good. Our 6 Nov vulkan.bin has four compute programs with
c4[0x90], c4[0xd0], c4[0x130] and c4[0x170] null, the slots PR 395 names, and ten more c4 slots. They
are not the PR's programs, whose hashes aren't in that file, and what they do isn't known.

=1 logs a slot that holds a mapped pointer now, once per program and slot, and changes nothing.
=2 also rebuilds the program from the live state, at most 4 times a run. The old pipeline stays alive
for work in flight. Unlike the PR, a rebuild is not written to vulkan.bin: a key's first entry wins on
load, so it would never be read. So =2 rebuilds again on each boot. The PR's load-time choice between
translations is not ported.

A PR 395 comment reports all grass gone in Hyrule Field on an RX 9070 XT, and its author saw the same.
Start with =1.

Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
